From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: battle for more than two duelists

Attack targets, the direct attack and battle damage now work with 3 and 4 duelists.
With 2 duelists every line keeps the stock text or gives the same value.

get_attack_target: the target list is the union of the zones of every living
opponent (turn order from the attacker). mcount_by counts the targets per duelist.
The direct attack mask (new card::direct_attack_mask) holds every living opponent
with no monster, or all of them with EFFECT_DIRECT_ATTACK or attack_player.
BattleCommand: battle_defender is set at target choice (the target's controller).
A direct attack with several open opponents asks the turn player with
MSG_SELECT_OPTION (0xFFFF0000 | duelist). MSG_ATTACK_DUELIST (201) follows the
MSG_ATTACK of a direct attack. The event player of EVENT_BE_BATTLE_TARGET is the
defender. opp_mzone (BattleCommand case 8, Adjust step 14, ChangeAttackTarget)
is the union over the living opponents. battle_defender is reset at 4 sites.
Forced attacks set the defender with no prompt. Patrician of Darkness: the
chooser is the owner of the effect. PRE_BATTLE_DAMAGE loops from the turn player.
calculate_battle_damage: a lambda other(x) replaces 1 - x (the stock form at n == 2).
Damage goes to the controller of the target or to battle_defender.
libduel: ChangeAttackTarget updates the defender and sends 201. GetBattleMonster
gives (nil, nil) to a duelist that is not in the battle.
common.h: the 200, 201, 202 message ids.

Not done here: the "defender eliminated" rollback (T5B), Duel.CalculateDamage
(DamageStep) for n > 2, damage reflect on opponent_of in operations.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
